<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 9 November, from 694 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">694 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,332 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Seventeenth Council of Toledo orders the enslavement of Jews</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Accusing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of conspiracy, the council called by King Egica decreed the enslavement of Jews in Visigothic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the removal of their children. It was among the harshest anti-Jewish measures of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1180">1180 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">846 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Minamoto no Yoritomo's forces rout the Taira at the Fuji River</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a night attack near the Fuji River, in present-day Shizuoka Prefecture, Minamoto forces of some 30,000 men under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo">Minamoto no Yoritomo</a> routed the Taira army of Taira no Koremori, who escaped. It was a battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genpei-war">Genpei War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo">Minamoto no Yoritomo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1313">1313 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">713 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis the Bavarian defeats Frederick the Fair at Gammelsdorf</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Duke Louis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-bavaria">Upper Bavaria</a> defeated his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-fair">Frederick the Fair</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, in a dispute over the guardianship of the young dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a>. The victory helped Louis's election as King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 1314.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gammelsdorf">Battle of Gammelsdorf</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-iv-holy-roman-emperor">Louis IV, Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-fair">Frederick the Fair</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1323">1323 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">703 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prataparudra surrenders Warangal, ending the Kakatiya dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning with reinforcements from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> after a failed first siege, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulugh-khan">Ulugh Khan</a>, the future sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-bin-tughluq">Muhammad bin Tughluq</a>, defeated and captured Prataparudra at the Kakatiya capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warangal">Warangal</a>. Prataparudra's surrender ended the Kakatiya dynasty, which had ruled most of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-bin-tughluq">Muhammad bin Tughluq</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1799">1799 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">227 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon's coup of 18 Brumaire topples the Directory</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> and his allies began a coup against the Directory, completed the next day. The new Consulate made Napoleon First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a> and effective ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wilhelm II's abdication is announced as Germany becomes a republic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With revolution spreading, Chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-maximilian-of-baden">Max von Baden</a> announced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a>'s abdication and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philipp-scheidemann">Philipp Scheidemann</a> proclaimed a republic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>. Wilhelm fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philipp-scheidemann">Philipp Scheidemann</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1938">1938 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kristallnacht: Nazi pogroms sweep Germany and Austria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Over two nights, Nazi mobs burned hundreds of synagogues, wrecked about 7,500 Jewish businesses and killed at least 91 people. About 30,000 Jewish men were sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Berlin Wall opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a confused announcement that East Germans could travel freely, crowds pressed the border crossings until guards opened the gates. The fall of the Wall led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-reunification">German reunification</a> within a year.</p></div></li></ol>
